# .claspignore — WHAT GOES UP TO APPS SCRIPT, AND NOTHING ELSE.
#
# The script project is THREE FILES: script.gs, app.html and appsscript.json.
# Everything else in this repo is scaffolding and none of it belongs in the
# editor.
#
# WITHOUT THIS FILE, `clasp push` UPLOADS ANY .js IT FINDS. clasp pushes every
# .js / .gs / .html / .json under rootDir, and each one lands in the editor as a
# script file — in the ONE GLOBAL SCOPE every .gs shares, which is the hazard
# this whole repo is shaped around. node_modules/ would follow them.
#
# clasp reads these as ignore patterns and pushes what is left, so the safe
# form is: ignore everything, then un-ignore the three files by name. Adding a
# fourth file to the project means adding it here — nothing else will tell you.
#
# THIS FILE ALONE DOES NOT ENABLE PUSHING. clasp also needs a .clasp.json
# carrying this deployment's scriptId, which is not committed because it is
# deployment-specific. `clasp clone <scriptId>` or `clasp login && clasp create`
# writes one; this file is what makes the push that follows safe.

**/**

!script.gs
!app.html
!appsscript.json
